abstract: >-
  Python pipeline that simulates the impact of a large constellation of
  orbital data center (ODC) satellites on Vera C. Rubin Observatory
  observations over a one-year window of the baseline survey. For each
  simulated pointing it (1) propagates satellite orbits with SGP4 for every
  orbital shell, (2) identifies satellites crossing the LSSTCam field of
  view, (3) computes streak brightness (AB magnitude and per-band surface
  brightness) from the sunlight-reflection geometry, with band corrections,
  (4) classifies streaks (ultrabright, saturated, unsaturated, faint) and
  computes the fraction of focal-plane pixels lost, including the summation
  of electrons from overlapping streaks, and (5) estimates the increase in
  whole-sky brightness relative to Rubin's natural sky-brightness model.
  Scripts for a 1/10th-scale constellation and notebooks for the summary
  statistics and analysis figures are included.

keywords:
  - satellite constellations
  - Vera C. Rubin Observatory
  - LSST
  - orbital data centers
  - satellite streaks
  - pixel loss
  - sky brightness
  - simulation
